{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795290365,"nonce":"8TP/eOxCHG5R8cQchDhCCJCBq3k=","title":"domain.from_array silently keeps only 3 coordinate columns of a wider array","message":"jno.domain.from_array({'data': a}) with a of shape (N, 66) gives dom.variable('data') returning 4 Variables (3 spatial + time); the other 63 columns are dropped with no error or warning. A dataset whose rows are high-dimensional samples (e.g. a discretised field per row for flow matching) is therefore silently truncated. Reproduce: len(jno.domain.from_array({'d': np.random.rand(10, 66)}).variable('d')) == 4. Workaround: attach the rows as a tensor, dom.variable('_rows', a[None, None]), and slice. Fix: raise when D \u003e 3 and name the tensor route.","files":null}]}